@startuml
title Device Credential Issuer — Pairing to MQTT Access (абстракции)

actor "Mobile App" as App
participant "Provisioning API" as Prov
participant "Credential Issuer" as Iss
participant "Device Registry" as Reg
participant "MQTT Broker\n(Admin/ACL)" as MQTT
participant "Device" as Dev

== Claim / Bind ==
App -> Prov: POST /devices/claim {claim_code, serial, household}
Prov -> Iss: validate claim & request credentials
Iss -> Reg: verify device(serial) & household ownership
Reg --> Iss: ok (device record or create)
Iss -> Iss: choose auth mode (mTLS or device-token)

alt mTLS certificate
  Iss -> Iss: generate short-lived client cert (X.509)\nsigned by IoT CA
  Iss -> MQTT: upsert ACL for deviceId (topics)
  Iss -> Reg: store cert meta / rotation_at
  Iss --> Prov: credentials {cert, clientId, mqttHost}
else device token
  Iss -> Iss: mint device access token (JWT/PASETO)\n+ refresh (short TTL)
  Iss -> MQTT: upsert ACL for deviceId (topics)
  Iss -> Reg: store token meta / rotation_at
  Iss --> Prov: credentials {token, clientId, mqttHost}
end

Prov --> App: credentials (secure channel)
App -> Dev: deliver credentials (BLE/SoftAP/DPP)

== Connect to MQTT ==
Dev -> MQTT: CONNECT (TLS), auth = cert/token
MQTT --> Dev: CONNACK (accepted)
Dev -> MQTT: publish state/subscribe commands
MQTT -> Reg: (optional) LWT/online status hook

== Rotations / Revoke ==
... later ...
Iss -> Reg: schedule rotation window
Iss -> MQTT: update ACL / revoke old cred
Dev -> MQTT: reconnect with new cred

note right
Идемпотентность на Iss/Reg.\nACL — минимальные темы per device.
claim_code одноразовый с TTL.
end note
@enduml